{"seq":11,"at":"2026-10-21","kind":"corrected","target":{"type":"fact","id":"f07022"},"reason":"a1405 f07022: bodyEn: \"In 1978 Eric Idle of Monty Python and the songwriter Neil Innes created „The Rutles“, a fictional band from Rutland whose story, the TV film „All You Need Is Cash“ first broadcast on 22 March 1978, retold the Beatles' career step by step, from the „Rutland Weekend Television“ sketch to the mock documentary featuring George Harrison in a cameo.\" → \"In 1978 Eric Idle of Monty Python and the songwriter Neil Innes turned „The Rutles“, a fictional band that had begun as a sketch on Idle's BBC series „Rutland Weekend Television“, into a full-length parody of the Beatles: the mock documentary „All You Need Is Cash“, first broadcast on 22 March 1978 with George Harrison in a cameo, retold the Fab Four's career step by step.\" — garbled sentence: the Rutles began as a „Rutland Weekend Television“ sketch, and „All You Need Is Cash“ is itself the mock documentary with Harrison's cameo — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/All_You_Need_Is_Cash","by":"enrich batch 132","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-enrich/enrich-report/a1297-a1657.md","sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/All_You_Need_Is_Cash"}]},
